# Jaspr Web Development Guide

## Core Mission

Expert Jaspr development assistant for modern, SEO-friendly websites using Dart. Leverage Flutter knowledge while mastering Jaspr-specific patterns.

## When to Use Jaspr

**✅ RECOMMEND for:**

- SEO-critical sites (marketing, blogs, docs)
- Server-side rendering (SSR) or static generation (SSG)
- Multi-page applications with fast loading
- Dart-first web development

**❌ AVOID for:**

- Mobile apps (use Flutter)
- Heavy client-side interactions (consider Flutter Web)
- JavaScript ecosystem dependencies

## Component Patterns

### Basic Component Structure

```dart
class MyComponent extends StatelessComponent {
  const MyComponent({required this.data, super.key});
  final DataType data;

  @override
  Iterable<Component> build(BuildContext context) sync* {
    yield div(classes: ['container'], [
      // Semantic HTML structure
    ]);
  }
}
```

### Semantic HTML Priority

```dart
// ✅ GOOD - Semantic structure
yield div([
  header([nav([/* navigation */])]),
  section([
    h1([text('Page Title')]),
    article([/* content */]),
  ]),
  footer([/* footer content */]),
]);
```

## Widget Granularity Guidelines

### Appropriate Widget Granularity

- **Prefer fewer, more cohesive widgets** over many tiny widgets
- Extract new widget classes only when they are:
  - **Reused in multiple places**
  - **Complex enough to warrant separation** (>50 lines)
  - **Logically independent** with clear boundaries
- For simpler UIs, use a single widget with well-commented sections

### Refactoring Decision Tree

Ask these questions in order:

1. **Is the component reused?** → Extract widget
2. **Is the component >50 lines?** → Consider extraction
3. **Is the component logically independent?** → Consider extraction
4. **Otherwise** → Keep in parent with comments

### Performance Considerations

- Be mindful that **each widget adds overhead**
- **Prefer fewer widgets** for simpler screens
- **Use const constructors aggressively**

### Examples

```dart
// ✅ GOOD - Single cohesive widget for simple UI
class ProfilePage extends StatelessComponent {
  const ProfilePage({required this.user, super.key});
  final User user;

  @override
  Iterable<Component> build(BuildContext context) sync* {
    yield div(classes: ['profile-page'], [
      // Header section
      header(classes: ['profile-header'], [
        img(src: user.avatarUrl, alt: 'Profile picture'),
        h1([text(user.name)]),
        p([text(user.bio)]),
      ]),

      // Stats section
      section(classes: ['profile-stats'], [
        div(classes: ['stat'], [
          span(classes: ['stat-number'], [text('${user.followers}')]),
          span(classes: ['stat-label'], [text('Followers')]),
        ]),
        div(classes: ['stat'], [
          span(classes: ['stat-number'], [text('${user.following}')]),
          span(classes: ['stat-label'], [text('Following')]),
        ]),
      ]),

      // Posts section
      section(classes: ['profile-posts'], [
        h2([text('Recent Posts')]),
        ...user.posts.map((post) => PostCard(post: post)), // Reused component
      ]),
    ]);
  }
}

// ✅ GOOD - Extract when reused
class PostCard extends StatelessComponent {
  const PostCard({required this.post, super.key});
  final Post post;

  @override
  Iterable<Component> build(BuildContext context) sync* {
    yield article(classes: ['post-card'], [
      h3([text(post.title)]),
      p([text(post.excerpt)]),
      time([text(post.publishedAt.toString())]),
    ]);
  }
}

// ❌ AVOID - Over-granular widgets for simple content
class ProfileHeaderTitle extends StatelessComponent {
  const ProfileHeaderTitle({required this.name, super.key});
  final String name;

  @override
  Iterable<Component> build(BuildContext context) sync* {
    yield h1([text(name)]); // Too simple to extract
  }
}
```

## Styling Strategy

### Native CSS (Recommended)

Use Jaspr's type-safe CSS system with `@css` annotations:

```dart
@css
final styles = [
  css('.hero')
    .background(color: Color(0xFF1a1a1a))
    .padding(Padding.symmetric(vertical: 4.rem, horizontal: 2.rem))
    .text(
      color: Colors.white,
      fontSize: 3.rem,
      fontWeight: FontWeight.bold,
      lineHeight: 1.2.px,
    )
    .styles(raw: const {
      'animation': 'fadeIn 0.5s ease-in-out',
      'backdrop-filter': 'blur(10px)',
    }),

  css('.card')
    .background(color: Colors.white)
    .border(Border.all(color: Color(0xFFe5e7eb), width: 1.px))
    .borderRadius(BorderRadius.circular(0.5.rem))
    .padding(Padding.all(1.5.rem))
    .boxShadow(BoxShadow(
      color: Color(0x1A000000),
      offset: Offset(0.px, 4.px),
      blurRadius: 6.px,
    ))
    .styles(raw: const {
      'aspect-ratio': '16/9',
      'object-fit': 'cover',
    }),

  // Responsive design with raw properties
  css.media(MediaQuery.screen(minWidth: 768.px), [
    css('.hero')
      .fontSize(4.rem)
      .styles(raw: const {
        'text-transform': 'uppercase',
        'letter-spacing': '0.1em',
      }),
    css('.grid')
      .display(Display.grid)
      .gridTemplate(
        columns: GridTracks([
          GridTrack.fr(1),
          GridTrack.fr(1),
        ]),
      )
      .styles(raw: const {
        'grid-gap': '2rem',
        'grid-auto-rows': 'minmax(200px, auto)',
      }),
  ]),

  // Animation keyframes using raw CSS
  css('@keyframes fadeIn', []).styles(raw: const {
    '0%': 'opacity: 0; transform: translateY(20px)',
    '100%': 'opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0)',
  }),

  css('@keyframes spin', []).styles(raw: const {
    '0%': 'transform: rotate(0deg)',
    '100%': 'transform: rotate(360deg)',
  }),
];
```

